From 0bdb102afd9d95ad3721d2469d667eb6df36e70a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: INTEL-CAMERA WIP <wip@localhost>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 14:24:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] BOZZA media: i2c: Add GC5035 image sensor driver

NON INVIABILE: tabelle registri segnaposto, V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN
limitato a 1x, attribuzione non sciolta, manca il Signed-off-by.
Vedi patches/wip/README.md nel progetto.

NON TESTATO su hardware: compila e passa checkpatch, nulla di piu'.
Il kernel che lo contiene non e' mai stato avviato.

Skeleton driver for the GalaxyCore GC5035, structured after gc05a2.c
with the x86/ACPI adaptations used by ov2740.c and t4ka3.c: ACPI match
table, optional reset/powerdown GPIOs, devm_v4l2_sensor_clk_get(),
8-bit CCI regmap with page banking via register 0xfe, and
enable_streams/disable_streams instead of the deprecated s_stream.

Target hardware: CHUWI Hi10 X1 (Intel N100, Alder Lake-N, IPU6),
ACPI HID GCTI5035 at \_SB.PC00.LNK1.
